At Fri, 4 Aug 2006 16:28:31 -0700 (PDT),
Christoph Lameter wrote:
> 
> Well the reason that I bought the cmipci card was because on board sound 
> does not work. It looks as if everything is working, I can toy around with 
> the mixer settings as much as I want. Still no sound. Tried multiple appls
> from commandline based mp3blaster to vlc and Rhythmbox. All are utterly 
> convinced that they have a great soundcard but no sound. I can plugin an 
> USB headset and it works just fine with both. I can plug the speakers into 
> a different computer and they just work fine.

VIA8237 has "VIA DXS" playback volumes.  They should be 100% (and are
so as default).

Otherwise, it's a problem of ac97 mixer setting for ALC655.
Please attach the generated file by "alsactl -f somefile store", and 
the contents of /proc/asound/card0/codec97#0/* files for further
checking.


